// Recurve bow arch, topological build. Root thickness = full
// tab width (26), tapering along the limb to an ~8 mm stalk that recurves
// at the tip. The tip is a solid rounded paddle (about 12 mm across) in
// place of the old curl-and-knob; the string loop sits in a 2.6 mm wide
// groove cut round the paddle's end and down both flanks, mid-thickness,
// down to a 7 mm post, so the pull goes into the paddle in compression
// and the lips above and below keep the loop from sliding off. The
// groove covers the half of the tip that faces the pull (the other limb)
// and the end; the neck is left solid. Through-bolted: 2x M4 clearance
// holes in the flange tab (heads counterbored on top; nuts live in hex
// pockets under the center piece).
limb2d = ✎ 0 0 70 2 140 16 185 40 202 51 212 66 206 80 205 82.3 201.5 88 198.5 87.5 195 87 191.8 83.5 192.5 79.5 193.2 77.5 197 76.5 199.5 74.5 204 66.9 195.8 57.5 179.8 49.1 135.3 30.2 67.5 23.9 0 26
limb   = limb2d |> extrude 14
groove = (tube 20 3.5 2.6 ∩ (box 40 40 4 |> move 20 0 0 |> rotz 60)) |> move 199 81 7
main = limb ⊖ groove
  |> at lft+fwd 0 27 3.5 (box 26 28 7)
  |> cutat lft+fwd 13 6 0 (zcyl 2.15 20)
  |> cutat lft+fwd 13 22 0 (zcyl 2.15 20)
  |> cutat lft+fwd 13 6 5.8 (zcyl 3.8 3)
  |> cutat lft+fwd 13 22 5.8 (zcyl 3.8 3)
